nodecode-web-search-plus is a rewrite of robbyczgw-cla's robbyczgw-cla/hermes-web-search-plus:
  https://github.com/robbyczgw-cla/hermes-web-search-plus
  commit 4eebfd77a4572111306f4ff551be4e53ef76f450
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Robby (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the plugin's two model-facing tools, web_search_plus and
web_extract_plus, and the behaviour behind them — routing a query to the
engine that suits its shape (Brave for general, Serper for security and
shopping, Exa for documentation and papers), falling back down the configured
providers when one fails or finds nothing, recency and news filters, domain
include and exclude lists, research mode (search, then read the top pages),
the provider chains for search and extraction, and the notes that say which
engine was tried and why it was skipped. The Python plugin is gone: the whole
cell is Common Lisp, and its network is nlk:http.

What was left out, and why: the engines and extractors whose API is not one
HTTP request to a documented endpoint — You.com, Linkup, Parallel, Keenable,
Serpbase, Querit, TinyFish, the Firecrawl search vertical, and the DonSeTch
CLI the original spawns — so a cell never runs a program on the operator's
machine. Also left out: the search cache and its persistence, the quality
report and routing diagnostics, provider health statistics, semantic span
ranking and query-intent classification, markdown as a second output format,
the setup and status slash commands of the Hermes CLI, and the native Hermes
web-provider bridge, which has no meaning outside its host.
